A||N||31||Jay||Northstar by Lexus?||||1||
Z||000000||Jay||07-12-2001||02:42 PM||||I was talking to a guy that works at Cadillac this week-end and he was saying that the Northstar was actually designed by Lexus, then bought by GM.  Anyone else heard of this?  If it is true, does the Lexus come in a stick shift and will it bolt up?  Something to think about I guess.||||reg||1
Z||000001||TylerB11||07-12-2001||03:59 PM||||If He said Lexus and its true - then he meant Toyota. Toyota fabricated the lexus name and company to compete in the luxury car market - if you buy a lexus you are getting a toyota with a lexus nameplate on it and a $15,000 increase on the pricetag. Same with Infinity & Nissan.<BR>Ain't nothing like paying for prestige.<BR>Atleast GM comes up with completely different cars for their cadillac line.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||KissMySSFiero||07-12-2001||04:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TylerB11:<BR><B><BR>Atleast GM comes up with completely different cars for their cadillac line.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>yeah like the Escalade!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  <BR>hehe.  i used to work as a tech at a cadi dealer.  ive never heard such a thing. but that doesnt mean its true.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||07-12-2001||04:08 PM||||What Toyota is the new IS300 or the older SC300.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wannabe||07-12-2001||04:14 PM||||I thought the Northstar design was an evolution of the Quad 4 and TDC designs, both of which were definitely GM concoctions. Also, Cadillac used the lessons learned from their earlier aluminum V8 blocks to design the Northstar block, or so I read in the SAE journal.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Will||07-12-2001||04:18 PM||||No, I'm almost certain that's not true.<P>Besides, Toyota/Lexus has their own line of V8's. The Lexus V8's are somewhat smaller than the Northstar externally and have belt driven cams with variable cam timing (Northstar has timing chains and fixed cam timing)||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||07-12-2001||04:36 PM||||Actually, GM and Toyota do have a partnership and it's possible some design elements came from (or were inspired by) Toyota. It wouldn't be all that surprizing.||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||07-12-2001||04:51 PM||||If GM designed the Northstar engine than chances are it would run like crap and brake down all the time. Probably wasn’t designed be GM! ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Slammed Fiero||07-12-2001||05:10 PM||||LS430, GS430 , and GS 300 all share parts. I believe the only one of these that trades major parts with the toyota line is the GS300 which utilizes a NA version of the supra motor <BR>LX470 is a landcrusier re badged<P>the IS300 is all new.<P>I forget the name of one of the older models , but it was a rebadged Camry.<BR>Remember the Nova?? of the late 80's haha all toyota. I have worked a bit for Lexus doing promotion and worked at GM doing research. Never heard that the Northstar was a Toyota motor.<P>Even if it was ..yee haa , Toyota makes damm good motors.<P>ohh here come the import car haters..haha<P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||07-12-2001||05:14 PM||||I don't think the NS is a Toyota engine, but it wouldn't surprise me if GM didn't get some idea's. I read the the NS came from the Quad 4 and DOHC work. They needed something they could market in the Caddy. It's not like it does anything amazing over the LS1 engines. Maybe a touch smoother.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Black88GT||07-12-2001||05:21 PM||||The early/mid 90s ES 300 I believe was the rebadged Camry.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Jay||07-12-2001||05:58 PM||||From what this guy said, there are a boat load of performance parts that will bolt onto the Northstar made by Toyota.  I'm gonna look into this a bit more, sounds interesting and plausible.||||reg||1
Z||000012||TRiAD||07-12-2001||07:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jay:<BR><B>From what this guy said, there are a boat load of performance parts that will bolt onto the Northstar made by Toyota.  I'm gonna look into this a bit more, sounds interesting and plausible.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>For that to be true, the N* would have to be a direct descendant of a Toyota/Lexus engine, and share many components. This much is obviously false. <P>The "Lexus" name exists ONLY in the US. The IS300 (only a 200 elsewhere) is actually the Toyota Altezza. The GS series and SC series all had other names in their other markets. The SCs were "Soarers" (and one of the top models had the Supra Turbo engine!)...can't remember the GS series' name. <P>The old Nova ("no-go" in Spanish) was a rebadged Corolla, the Geo Metro was Suzuki, but the Prism was also a Corolla, The Tracker was also Suzuki. There was talk of the RAV4 becomming a Tracker, before "Geo" was killed, and GM decided to just continue with Suzuki. <P>Oh, Ford Fiestas were German, the Festivas were Kias, as is the Aspire (ugh!). The Pontiac LeMans? Opel Kadett. (So there is precedence for the Opel Speedster to become a GM-badged product.)<P><BR>Here's an Opel Kadett (Pontiac LeMans) with Rieger's "GTO" WideBodyKit. <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.opel-gang.de/OPELz/KL-DT972/Pics/GSiCabrioKL-DT972_93-12-dasErgebnis.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000013||Wolfhound||07-12-2001||08:12 PM||||Patten use rights for the Kawasaki 900 DOHC head design were bought from Alfa Romao!<BR>That's a fact.||||reg||1
Z||000014||lowCG||07-12-2001||10:03 PM||||I've got a '92 SC400,love the buttery smooth power,and the sporty ride as the chassis is mostly Turbo Supra.<BR>Doesn't compare to the old Fiero though with the mid-engined action.<BR>Too bad the"Northstar Sytem" doesn't have variable cam timing.<BR>I saw an old Mercedes 190sl(small convertible) with a 4.0 Lexus/Toyota V8 in it,right around 300hp the way it was installed with no cats,K&N intake,air/fuel controller.||||reg||1
Z||000015||Songman||07-13-2001||12:47 AM||||I know Toyota created Lexus, but my V8 LS400 is far from being a Toyota. Think what you want. The best Toyota ever made doesn't even come close!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000016||artherd||07-13-2001||04:51 AM||||I cannot off the top of my head actually think of one dimention that any toyota (Lexus does not make engines) V8 that shares any dimention or spec with the Northstar V8...<P>BOre stroke, bearing, seal, rod, valve, water/oil port sizes...<P>I also belive the design was "internal" to GM for the mostpart, however that would not nessicarily preclude participation in the design of subcontractors (infact anything so complex as a modern IC engine will all but requre such practice.)<P>I do know the things are practically bulletproof, which is more of a classically japanese idea than american, however they're also quite powerful...<P>Is is possible we could have the best of both worlds here?<P>(and is anyone else puzzled as to why the Northstar hasn't made it out of, pardon my french, grandma-mobiles? Shortstar not withstanding (certinly not anymore...)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000017||TylerB11||07-13-2001||08:45 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B>I know Toyota created Lexus, but my V8 LS400 is far from being a Toyota. Think what you want. The best Toyota ever made doesn't even come close!<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So how is your Toyotal Avalon..err LS400   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I didn't mean to step on any toes with my original post. The only real difference between most toyota's and lexus's (besides the emblem and price tag, hehe) Is Lexus offers Luxury packages that toyota doesn't. <P>Don't be offended - People that get into a porche will realize its nothing more than a VW on steriods(I used to own a 911. Nice car, not built like the price tag)<p>[This message has been edited by TylerB11 (edited 07-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||erikred||07-13-2001||10:03 AM||||Now we know that Japan and Germany are the only countries that can make cars, and that the Lexus is THE current status symbol for the fickle public. If Caddilac has a Lexus engine then it might just be reliable enough to consider buying. After all,what do most potential Lexus buyers think? "Cannot go wrong with Japanese reliability" and "Sure would be nice to be able to say I have a Lexus". So if there just happened to be a rumor started that Lexus designed the caddy's engine, sales men just might make a little more in comission.<P>In reality the Northstar is the Oldsmobile Aurora v8 which was designed after the Oldsmobile Quad4 which was at least partialy inspired by the Cosworth-Vega DOHC 16v 4cyl. BTW, contrary to popular belief the Japanese are not great inovators, they just have different laws which allow them to exploit nearly everything for the good of their industry.||||reg||8
Z||000019||Mr.Frosty||07-13-2001||10:03 AM||||AMEN Tyler,<BR> As for who said Toyotas share nothing with the Lexus line,the LEXUS IS300 "IS" the "TOYOTA" Altezza in Japan.As far as I know they don't have a Lexus designation in Japan for it,it's just a plain 'OL "Altezza" I don't know what the rest of the world calls it,but here it's a rebadged "TOYOTA".   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled<p>[This message has been edited by Mr.Frosty (edited 07-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000020||TRiAD||07-13-2001||10:20 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TylerB11:<BR><B>...People that get into a porche will realize its nothing more than a VW on steriods(I used to own a 911. Nice car, not built like the price tag)...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>OK, there's this enduring idea that Porsche and VW have a similar relationship to that of Toyota/Lexus. This is simply not the case. <BR>Now, yes, several Porsches have been built by VW/Audi (under contract) in the past...The 914, 924, 944...And now they are sharing a platform for their "SUV". <B>BUT</B>, Porsche and VW are completely seperate companies with their own agendas. <BR>VW did get it's start with/from Porsche, and Ferdinand Porsche's grandson is the current CEO of VAG (VW/Audi Group, which includes Skoda, Lamborghini, Bugatti, Bentley, and others), but they are seperate. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 07-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000021||87ECO5||07-13-2001||10:34 AM||||It's all marketing.<P>There's no Lexus, Infinity, or Acura anywhere else in the world!  We, as Americans, in the ongoing effort to out do everyone else, must have a special marque for our Toyotas, Nissans and Hondas.||||reg||1
Z||000022||rc5star||07-13-2001||10:43 AM||||Their are 2 guys at my work that were on the design team for the northstar engine and they both said that it was a GM design. I dont know if they are 100% correct but that is what they said. Who knows GM might actually have made a good engine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. ||||reg||1
Z||000023||terryk||07-13-2001||10:48 AM||||When I was in Japan, I noticed they were "Honda Legends"........||||reg||1
Z||000024||Slammed Fiero||07-13-2001||10:56 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B>  <BR>OK, there's this enduring idea that Porsche and VW have a similar relationship to that of Toyota/Lexus. This is simply not the case. <BR>Now, yes, several Porsches have been built by VW/Audi (under contract) in the past...The 914, 924, 944...And now they are sharing a platform for their "SUV". [b]BUT</B>, Porsche and VW are completely seperate companies with their own agendas. <BR>VW did get it's start with/from Porsche, and Ferdinand Porsche's grandson is the current CEO of VAG (VW/Audi Group, which includes Skoda, Lamborghini, Bugatti, Bentley, and others), but they are seperate. <P><BR>[This message has been edited by TRiAD (edited 07-13-2001).][/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>VW and Porsche broke off permanent ties a while back. Although they do share some intrests VW has nothing to do with Porsche Design ..espically the 911. (thank you triad for setting things straight)<P>While the VW beetle and the porsche once shared the same initial boxer engine , air cooled design , there was no relationship technically between the 2, except in the original prototypes of the 356 'bathtub" cars<P>Want a real relationship?? From 1960 to 1969 Ferry Porsche (sp) was given a Brand new corvair for his aid in the design of the car. There are lots of pics of him floating around driving his 69 gold 140hp 4spd corvair , that he keeps (kept?) at his personal residence.<P>Now thats a little known fact!<BR> <P><P>------------------<BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals, White face Gauges , 70Hp Shot of NOS Autocrossed , Tracked , Dragged? (soon) abused.||||reg||1
Z||000025||MoneypitGT||07-13-2001||09:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>contrary to popular belief the Japanese are not great inovators, they just have different laws which allow them to exploit nearly everything for the good of their industry.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That is exactly right, In japan you can only hold a patent for i think 5 years, so everyone just builds off each other.<BR>To add to the list of GM/Toyota venture, the new Pontiac Vibe is a Celica GTS, (basically) GM is closing the Prizm line to build the Vibe, completly Toyota. Oh and the Toyota version is the Matrix, I'm sure you have heard about it. As far as Toyota designing the N*, if Toyota had anything to do with it, it was a Toyota product that GM tried to copy and that's about it. The N* is definatley built off the QUAD, it even has the headgasket problem (although no where near as bad), and that I can personally vouch for.<BR> Chris<BR>PS I love my QUAD.<P>------------------<BR><B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>2 '87 GT Projects||||reg||3
Z||000026||qwikgta||07-13-2001||10:04 PM||||GM and Toyota have a deal to always have a car designed and sold by each other.  It will become the Vibe/Matrix next year as an 03 model.  I like the look of the Vibe and I like the 180hp/6 spd/18" rims idea.  I will be getting one as soon as I can.  <P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||Songman||07-14-2001||12:15 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TylerB11:<BR><B>  So how is your Toyotal Avalon..err LS400     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I didn't mean to step on any toes with my original post. The only real difference between most toyota's and lexus's (besides the emblem and price tag, hehe) Is Lexus offers Luxury packages that toyota doesn't. <P>Don't be offended - People that get into a porche will realize its nothing more than a VW on steriods(I used to own a 911. Nice car, not built like the price tag)<P>[This message has been edited by TylerB11 (edited 07-13-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Don't worry. I'm not offended. And I did go look up the Toyota Avalon. It does look like the new Lexus LS400. But the biggest engine you can get in it is a 24 valve V6. Also, my car is a 93. Toyota made nothing even close then...<P>And after owning three 911s, I do admit that they are not really worth the price tag if you are looking for daily transportation but if I was looking for that I would buy a Taurus. As for it being a VW on steroids. They would have to be some might big steroids. I don't think you could build that flat-4 to come anywhere close to the Porsche 6, not to mention handling. I admit the engineering is the same, but so are most cars but we don't say they are all the same..<P>Don't worry... I'm with you on what you are saying, just not on some of the finer points. If I agreed on the finer points I would have to like my old 84 SE parts car just as much as I like my Indy Pace Car. Or a regular Monte Carlo SS as much as I like my Aerocoupe. Special editions are built for a reason. A Lexus is a special edition Toyota and therefore should cost more just like my other examples cost more.. they just happen to make the Lexus every year...<P>To tie in to the original post... I am fairly sure, as seems to be the consensus, that the Northstar is a GM invention.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 07-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000028||lowCG||07-14-2001||10:51 AM||||My Lexus reminded me of an old Ford after I got it back from the dealer for some service;they left off hose clamps,left wires dangling everywhere.<BR>From what I've noticed,the brand name will offer at least one model that's not currently available here in the states.<BR>Back in the eighties,we(I)could only dream of that,or go to one of those junkyards and get an engine from over there(2TG)and put it into the export car(Corolla).||||reg||1
Z||000029||Will||07-14-2001||02:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MoneypitGT:<BR><B> That is exactly right, In japan you can only hold a patent for i think 5 years, so everyone just builds off each other.<BR>To add to the list of GM/Toyota venture, the new Pontiac Vibe is a Celica GTS, (basically) GM is closing the Prizm line to build the Vibe, completly Toyota. Oh and the Toyota version is the Matrix, I'm sure you have heard about it. As far as Toyota designing the N*, if Toyota had anything to do with it, it was a Toyota product that GM tried to copy and that's about it. The N* is definatley built off the QUAD, it even has the headgasket problem (although no where near as bad), and that I can personally vouch for.<BR> Chris<BR>PS I love my QUAD.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have never heard anything about the Northstar having head gasket problems. What I have heard of the Northstar is that it has absolutely bulletproof reliability.<BR>I have 7 warranteed Northstar longblocks in my engine shed; they were warranteed for reasons varying from broken accessory mounting bosses, to leaking coolant from block porosity, to a broken con rod at 62 miles.<P>None of them were warranteed for head gasket trouble.||||reg||1
Z||000030||Black88GT||07-14-2001||03:31 PM||||For the people saying that such and such lexus or Acura is a such and such Toyota or Honda in Japan means nothing to me.  I don't live in Japan.  In the good old U.S. of A.(Canada too I think), the IS300 is a Lexus car that shares nothing with any Toyota that I can buy.  Yes I understand its a Toyota product, just like Caddy's are GM's and Lincoln's are Ford's.  But the IS300 is unique to Lexus as far as this american citizen is concerned.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000031||artherd||07-15-2001||03:25 AM||||"They're going to destroy the whole WORLD!!!"<P>"Phew, I'm glad I live in America!"<P>"Fry, America is PART of the world!!"<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
